      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Crossing over",
      "body": "**Crossing over**: the return trip of thumb under. Coming down with the right hand, after the thumb plays, finger 3 reaches over it to the next key, and the hand follows.\n\n**Why it matters:** it brings a run back down as smoothly as it went up.\n\nPress **Watch**: C, B, A, G, F with fingers 5 to 1, then finger 3 crosses over to E.",
